.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		ECCE-QM, B3LYP-D3(BJ)/def2-SVPD, charge -1, transition-state optimisation and frequencies, orbitals localised. This calculation shows the E2 transition state, with one imaginary mode at -586.84 cm-1, the transferring hydrogen anti-periplanar to the chlorine (H-C-C-Cl 180.0 degrees; C-H 1.303 Å, H-F 1.275 Å, C-Cl 2.113 Å, C-C 1.437 Å), and an electronic energy of -638.908578 Eh, 8.1 kJ/mol above the reactant complex.
